<title>AUSTRIA: FORECAST - IHS details Austria 5-yr economic outlook.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - IHS details Austria 5-yr economic outlook.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Institute for Advanced Studies (IHS), a leading Austrian economic research institute, revealed the following five-year forecasts for the country's economy on Friday.</p>
<p>(figures are average growth rate in percent)</p>
<p>					   1997-2001  1992-1996</p>
<p> Gross domestic product		 2.1	  1.7</p>
<p> Private consumption		    1.4	  1.8</p>
<p>   Durable goods			  1.2	  0.4</p>
<p>   Non-durable goods		    1.4	  2.0</p>
<p> Gross investment in fixed assets   2.0	  2.0</p>
<p>   Equipment				4.7	  1.1</p>
<p>   Building				-0.3	  2.5</p>
<p> Domestic demand			  1.6	  2.3</p>
<p> Exports				    6.0	  2.8</p>
<p>   Goods				    6.9	  4.2</p>
<p>   Tourism				  0.5	 -4.5</p>
<p> Imports				    5.0	  4.1</p>
<p>   Goods				    5.5	  3.9</p>
<p>   Tourism				  1.1	  7.0</p>
<p> Unemployment rate (absolute)	 7.4	  6.6</p>
<p> Disposable income (nominal)	  3.4	  4.3</p>
<p> GDP price index			  2.0	  3.0</p>
<p> Consumer price index		   2.2	  3.0</p>
<p> Money supply M1			  2.8	  8.7</p>
<p> Current account (bln schillings) -26.0	 -25.6</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom, +431 531 12 254</p>
</text>
